	(uuid "64afd8dc-8aca-5289-8605-504078556af8")
	(paper "A0")
	(title_block
		(title "HIGH VOLTAGE: H-bridge (4 x 3.3 kV SiC), R_S + L_S with freewheel diodes, gated push-pull high-side drive, low-side drivers, current sense and comparators, bridge test load")
		(date "2026-11-27")
		(rev "A-draft")
		(company "Open AED project — CERN-OHL-S-2.0 — NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION")
		(comment 1 "NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION — unreviewed design")
		(comment 2 "Source: docs/HARDWARE_DESIGN.md v0.3 §B6, §B13.5, §B14; contract.md issue 3; rev3-changes.md WP-G; capture notes WP-G.md")
		(comment 3 "Every turn-off is low side first (sheet 12 orders it); coil current freewheels through D1302+D1301; no switch is ever allowed to avalanche.")
		(comment 4 "Every switch is held OFF by a gate-source resistor with all supplies absent. HV_*, HSA_*, HSB_* nets carry up to 2.2 kV: no test points on them (R9).")
		(comment 5 "Revision 0.3 (contract issue 3): 80 A over-current trip, fast 3 A idle path IDLE_FAST_N, carrier-loss detectors on both high-side islands, LSD_OK monitor of the +20 V low-side supply, 75 nF local film capacitor HV_CAP_P-HV_RTN, I_SHOCK 24.0 mV/A. Simulated check: sim/rev3-wpg/notes.md.")
		(comment 6 "Generated by tools/schgen from the sheet spec — edit the spec, not this file (until schematic freeze)")
	)
