	(text_box "H-bridge: four 3.3 kV SiC MOSFETs (Microchip MSC080SMA330B4N, TO-247-4 with source sense)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(size 154.52 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ac3ae025-9339-5533-992d-72334d6c1cbc")
	)
	(text_box "Phase 1: QHA on beforehand (carrier), QLB times the pulse. Phase 2: QHB on beforehand, QLA times it (§B6.1). High sides switch at zero\ncurrent; low sides switch the current. VDSS 3300 V against <= 2.2 kV (1.5x). Gate drive returns to each device's SOURCE SENSE pin\n(terminal 3), never to the power source.\nThermal [CALC from DS00005914A Fig 1-5, 1-18; capture notes §4]: worst planned shock (65.7 A decaying, 25 Ohm, phase 1 = 3-12 ms) Tj 55\n-> 102 C at VGS 20 V, -> 119 C if a high side only reaches VGS 17 V; fault 'low side frozen on to the 28.8 ms cap' 2,000 V, 25 Ohm: 124\nC worst. Limit 150 C. Fault 18 (QLB shorted, QHA turning on slowly through its linear region) is NOT covered: 130-300 C estimated ->\nfinding F-1.\nNo avalanche and no short-circuit rating exist for this part: the design never lets it avalanche (freewheel D1301/D1302) and the OC\nlatch trips at 82-98 A, but the current at the instant of turn-off (115-126 A) is above IDM 107 A -> finding F-2.\nREVISION 0.3: OC trip 80 A (band 74-86 A, R1351 196 k): interrupted current 86-97 A [SIM sim/rev3-wpg S-2] below IDM. Fault 18 /\nsame-side shoot-through are now ended by the fast idle path + the sheet-12 kill latch + the carrier-loss detectors: QHA energy and\njunction estimates in sim/rev3-wpg/notes.md S-1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 154.52 27.908)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "eab5415a-fb7f-5408-844c-60cab8f80862")
	)
	(text_box "Series element R_S + L_S, freewheel diodes D1302 + D1301 (two in series), snubber C1301 + C1302 + R1304"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 200.24 25.4 0)
		(size 245.46 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dc84ef45-bbfc-5425-92eb-e192925c0ce3")
	)
	(text_box "R1301 R_S 3.9 Ohm ceramic composition (Ohmite OY39GKE, 80 J single impulse): 23.6 J per adult shock at 25 Ohm, 3.3 J at 175 Ohm [CALC]; 254 V peak across it (400 V working). L1301 30 uH made to order (§14).\nFreewheel: anode at HV_BUS, cathode at HV_CAP_P (§B6.5). TWO 3.3 kV SiC Schottky diodes in series (departure: the contract lists one D1301): a single shorted freewheel diode would otherwise silently remove R_S and L_S\nfrom the circuit. Each GC05MPS33J: 3300 V, IF,MAX 250 A for 10 us; stress 24 A (phase end) to about 126 A (OC trip) decaying with tau = 7.6 us.\nSnubber HV_BUS-HV_RTN: two 10 nF 3 kV X7R MLCC in series (5 nF nominal, about 2.5-3.5 nF at 2 kV bias [EST]) + 10 Ohm OY. Two in series so that one cracked/shorted MLCC does not short the capacitor through R_S. Values\nare placeholders for simulation [SIM] (§B6.5)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 200.24 31.75 0)
		(size 245.46 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a01f5256-5356-5ab0-b3f4-67e6fc38145b")
	)
	(text_box "QLA low-side drive: UCC5350MC (Miller clamp), +20/-5 V, Rg_on 220 Ohm, Rg_off 33 Ohm + diode"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 466.02 25.4 0)
		(size 247.1 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
