	(text_box "MGJ2 output 0 V (LSD_0V) joins each low side's SOURCE SENSE through its own 2.2 Ohm (R1320, R1325) so the two Kelvin loops are not joined directly through LS_SRC. Each driver has its own 1 uF\nfrom +20 V and to -5 V at its Kelvin source.\nPRELOADS (capture addition): the MGJ2 needs >= 10 % load or its output rises up to 1.25 x (20 V -> 25 V, above VGS max 23 V) (Murata KDC_MGJ2_F01 'Minimum load'). R1326 2.2 k on +20 V (9.1 mA >=\n8 mA) and R1327 1.2 k on -5 V (4.2 mA >= 4 mA).\nHold-up: 10 uF + 2 x 1 uF on each rail, preload tau about 26 ms: the drivers stay above UVLO2 (11 V max falling) for about 20 ms after BRIDGE_5V is lost, far longer than the low-side-first\nturn-off (about 1 us) needs. Start-up 5.4 ms typ (inside RAIL_READY 20 ms on 12)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 733.44 103.219 0)
		(size 220.01 14.954)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
