	)
	(text_box "U1304 astable: RA 12.4 k, RB 2.74 k, C 100 pF C0G -> high 1.05 us, low 0.19 us, 805 kHz nominal [CALC; 650-900 kHz with parts and 555 delay EST]. U1305 inverts; U1306 toggles on OSC falling edges -> PH1/PH2 at about 400 kHz,\nexactly 50 % (equal volt-seconds in the transformer).\nU1307/U1308 (sync): G_HA/G_HB is sampled on the PH1 rising edge so the carrier always starts with a whole cycle (§B6.3 'gating on a clock edge'); /CLR = G_H* stops it at once (adds <= 2.5 us to turn-on, nothing to turn-off).\nDrive = PHx AND OSC AND EN (U1309-U1312): each FET conducts about 1.05 us per 2.5 us period, with 0.19 us dead time at every phase change (no cross-conduction in the centre-tapped primary). Everything runs whenever BRIDGE_3V3\nis up; the gate pull-downs and the 100 k on G_H* make every input low when 12 is unpowered."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 133.475 0)
		(size 257.09 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
