	(text_box "T1301 secondary -> 1N4148W bridge -> HSA_RECT (1 nF, 2.2 k bleed, 20 V zener clamp) -> diode -> 100 Ohm -> gate. 2 x 47 nF C0G\ngate-source (one open still leaves 47 nF) + Cgs about 3.46 nF = 97.5 nF.\nTurn-on [CALC]: tau = (100 + about 5) Ohm x about 103 nF effective (incl. the MOSFET's own charge to 15 V) = 10.8 us; 0 -> 15 V from\nan 18.3 V source in 18.5 us nominal; worst (17.3 V source, +20 Ohm source resistance, C +5 %): 26.4 us + 2.5 us sync + 1.3 us = <= 30\nus (spec <= 40 us).\nTurn-off [CALC]: carrier stops -> HSA_RECT collapses (tau 2.2 us; PNP starts after about 0.2 us) -> BC807-40 pulls the gate through\n22 Ohm, base drive via 470 Ohm + 2.2 k: tau 2.8 us nominal, 4.0 us worst -> below 2 V in 7.1 us nominal / <= 10.3 us worst; below 1 V\nin <= 15.4 us worst (spec about 10 us, <= 20 us). PNP failed open: 10 k bleed, tau 0.98 ms.\nOff state: the PNP also clamps any Miller-coupled rise to about 0.6-1.5 V. dv/dt coupling 51 nC / 97.5 nF = 0.52 V (one 47 nF open:\n1.0 V, PNP clamp about 1.4 V) against VGS(th) minimum 1.9 V at 25 C, about 1.48 V at 150 C [EST from Fig 1-16 scaling] (capture notes\n§5).\nD1319 22 V gate clamp (backup to the 20 V clamp on HSA_RECT). R1332 10 k holds the gate off with no carrier."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 973.77 160.877 0)
		(size 151.23 27.908)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
