	(text_box "Over-current (rev 0.3, G-1): shunt Kelvin -> 100 Ohm / 1 nF (tau 100 ns) -> TLV3501 (4.5 ns). Threshold 3.3 V x 10.0 k / 206 k = 160.2 mV, referred to the shunt's own HV_RTN Kelvin terminal -> 80.1 A nominal; band about 74-86 A\nwith reference +-2.9 %, offset +-6.5 mV, shunt +-1 % and TCR [CALC]. Interrupted current 86-97 A at 2,200 V [SIM sim/rev3-wpg S-2]; highest planned peak 67.4 A (2,000 V, 25 Ohm).\nWaveform (rev 0.3, G-2): INA240A1 (gain 20) on BRIDGE_5V, 10 Ohm input resistors, divider 13.3 k / 20.0 k (x 0.6006) -> I_SHOCK = 24.0 mV/A; saturated output (VS - 0.2 V) x 0.6006 <= 3.20 V at BRIDGE_5V 5.5 V, below the main\ncontroller's VDDA minimum 3.26 V (§B6.6, LR §5.1).\nIdle current (slow path, kept): I_SHOCK -> 1 k / 100 pF -> TLV3501, threshold 3.3 V x 10.0 k / 277 k = 119.1 mV -> 4.96 A. It depends on the INA240: a dead INA240 reads 0 A, which the self-test catches (no current in the test\nsequence). The fast path (group idfast) is the primary idle detector from rev 0.3; this one stays as an independent, slower second.\nD1303 (capture addition): S3D across the shunt. If the 2 mOhm shunt ever opens, LS_SRC would otherwise rise to kilovolts and destroy both low-side drivers, the MGJ2 and the INA240; with D1303 it stays below about 1 V and the OC\ncomparator trips at once (fail safe, detected).\nBAT54S clamps the OC comparator input to GND/BRIDGE_3V3. Outputs are push-pull on BRIDGE_3V3; the 100 k pull-downs are on 12: unpowered or open = 'fault' (R11)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 302.81 236.664 0)
		(size 261.36 21.431)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
