	(text_box "Each divider (997 kOhm) is also the output's rest pull-down. Idle: off-state leakage of the high side (<= 35 uA at 3.3 kV, 25 C) x 997 k <= 35 V on the output, <= 35 mV on the tap; a shorted high side\nreads the capacitor voltage / 997 (<= 2.2 V).\nPer resistor: 550 V at 2.2 kV (one shorted: 733 V) against 3000 V working; 1.2 W only while the output is at full voltage (ms in a shock; seconds in the 'high side shorted' fault) against 1 W rated and\n2.5 x rated voltage for 5 s overload.\nTaps clamped to GND at the tap (BZX84C3V6, R-21), not to a reader's rail."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
