	)
	(text_box "Input filter R1365 100 Ohm / C1345 100 pF (tau 10 ns). Closes the shorted-low-side gap (fault 18 and the same-side shoot-through, BR Q1): sheet 12 ORs IDLE_FAST_N with IDLE_I_DET_N, arms it only after both low sides\nhave been off for 9 us, and the kill latch removes G_HA/G_HB in about 45 ns.\nThreshold [CALC]: pedestal 3.3 x 100/10,100 = 32.67 mV; reference 3.3 x 1.00/7.73 = 426.9 mV = 11 x 38.81 mV -> (38.81 - 32.67) mV / 2 mOhm = 3.07 A falling-edge reference, 3.20 A rising with the 6 mV hysteresis. Both\nratiometric to BRIDGE_3V3. Band 2.54-3.87 A worst case (TLV3501 +-6.5 mV / 11 dominates; OPA838 -230/+220 uV; 0.1 % parts; shunt 2.3 %).\nDepartures from G-3 (capture notes rev 0.3): R1364 pedestal added (the OPA838 output cannot reach below 0.1-0.2 V, SBOS867E VOL, so without it the comparator would see 'current' at zero current); R1366/R1367 1.00\nk/100 Ohm instead of 10.0 k/1.00 k (bias-current balance); D1332 single BAT54 to GND instead of BAT54S (leakage from BRIDGE_3V3).\nNormal shocks stay linear (65.7 A -> 1.80 V; saturation at 125 A). Simulated (sim/rev3-wpg S-1, S-3): shorted low side ended at 9-25 mJ in QHA; no false trip in a normal sequence or with the charger running, margin >=\n1.67 A above the band bottom. GND of U1317/U1318 must be taken at SHUNT_KN (layout requirement L-1, capture notes)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 413 0)
		(size 245.045 19.272)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
