	(text_box "Without it an MGJ2-only failure lets the low-side gate sag through 9-12 V while the switch carries up to 50 A (BR Q4: 158-181 C). LSD_OK low ends the sequence through sheet 12 (RAIL_OK) like a BRIDGE_5V collapse and blocks a\nstart.\nTrip [CALC]: 1.827 V x 112.1/12.1 = 16.93 V; band 16.45-17.35 V (BRIDGE_3V3 +-1.5 %, four 0.1 % resistors, TLV7031 offset +-8 mV and hysteresis 2-17 mV x 9.26, SLVSE13J). Normal rail 19.5-22 V; lowest working input (BRIDGE_5V\n4.5 V, MGJ2 line regulation 1.2 %/%) about 18.1 V [EST]: margin about 0.75 V. Sensed against GND: the LS_SRC offset (<= 0.17 V at 86 A) only raises the reading.\nThe -5 V rail is not monitored (capture notes, failure table)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 584.49 420.02 0)
		(size 257.835 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
